    "waveform": "carrier-period",
    "notes": "Every command is lowered to the press, hold and release waveform records the 650 shares with the Harmony One (ir_lowering.py)."
  },
  "notes": "The Harmony 650 and 665 (one remote under two skins, 72 and 75), and the Harmony 600 (71, 73 in Europe), the same firmware program with a grey screen: architecture 14, a 128x128 screen with keys beside it and no touchscreen, on AA batteries. A 600 build takes the 600's own grey pictures and light levels (scaffolds/harmony-600). Configurations are generated from the project alone (backends/harmony_650/compose.py) onto a scaffold drawn from Logitech's own: the Activities menu and Devices list, each device's and activity's pages, Starting and Turning off, the sending mark, Help and Help held's Delay Fixing, favourite channels. Twelve testers' configurations import, rebuild and import the same. Not yet: favourites' logos. Learning is off: the 650 can learn, but Afterglow does not drive it yet.",
  "schema": "afterglow-remote/1",
